    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d5">

                <pb facs="0011" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">641.5531/19: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador to the Belgian Government in Exile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-04-30T22:00:00+02:00">April 30, 1942—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 30—7:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Belgian Series No. 3. Your 2, April 28, 7 p.m. I have spoken in a preliminary way
                    to Belgian Colonial Minister de Vleeschauwer <pb facs="0012" n="6" xml:id="pg6"
                    /> regarding problem of Congo purchases and supplies and he is postponing
                    contemplated trip to Washington.</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Biddle</hi>
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
